  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Exact ZZ[x] and QQ[x] resource construction and coefficient export now use one canonical variable-length SJPZ/SJPQ payload instead of one generated FFI call per coefficient. New symmetric runtime codecs preserve arbitrary per-entry skew, canonical signs, trailing-zero normalization, native-disabled behavior, and malformed-input rejection. The focused benchmark measures degree-20000 ZZ construction/export at 6.0/0.94 ms and degree-10000 QQ at 13.4/12.5 ms on the handoff host, versus scalar-boundary baselines of 118/107 ms and 59/99 ms. The integration also minimally registers the pre-existing dense integer solve resource test in the host-test manifest, repairing the unrelated portable-tier inventory drift exposed by final validation.",
    "risks": [
      "The existing deserialize ABI transports the complete byte stream through one nonnegative exact Integer, requiring a linear byte copy and BigInt conversion; a future declared byte-region input could remove that transport copy without changing the canonical SJP representation."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "Integrate bench/exact-polynomial-bulk-io.cjs into the central benchmark catalog or performance runner from the integration lane.",
      "Consider a generated read-only byte-region input ABI when boundary-copy profiles show it is worthwhile."
    ]
  }
